Fix batch truncation in _causal_conv1d_fir introduced by tenstorrent/tt-metal#53320.

#53320 replaced a Python slice with an explicit ttnn.slice to keep the rm_only
hop in DRAM (a sound fix for an L1 OOM at bank_manager.cpp:451). But writing the
bounds out by hand pinned the BATCH end to a literal 1, so every user past the
first is silently discarded whenever B >= 2.

Symptom, on a 1x2 Blackhole mesh (2x p150a, "P300") running qwen36 at TP=2:

    tt/gdn/tp.py:934  q = ttnn.slice(conv, (0, 0, 0), (B, T, kd))
    RuntimeError: TT_FATAL @ slice_device_operation.cpp:126:
      args.slice_end[i] <= tensor_args.input.padded_shape()[i]
      Ends 2 must be less than or equal to the shape of the tensor 1

conv arrives as Shape([1, 128, 5120]) where [2, 128, 5120] is required. The
downstream slice is correct; the truncation happens upstream in the FIR.

Verified on silicon with this one-character change:

    3 passed, 10 deselected in 112.57s
    batched GDN prefill (B=2)        PCC min=0.99999 max=1.00000  lens=[128, 96]
    batched chunk-outer carry (B=2)  PCC min=1.00000 max=1.00000
    batched GDN prefill (B=4)        PCC min=0.99998 max=1.00000  lens=[128, 96, 64, 128]

--- a/models/experimental/gated_attention_gated_deltanet/tt/ttnn_gated_deltanet.py
+++ b/models/experimental/gated_attention_gated_deltanet/tt/ttnn_gated_deltanet.py
@@ -219,7 +219,7 @@ def _causal_conv1d_fir(
     out = None
     for k in range(kernel_size):
-        x_slice = ttnn.slice(x_padded, (0, k, 0), (1, k + T, D), memory_config=_dram)
+        x_slice = ttnn.slice(x_padded, (0, k, 0), (B, k + T, D), memory_config=_dram)
         if k != 0:
             x_slice = ttnn.to_layout(x_slice, ttnn.TILE_LAYOUT)
         if out is None:
